[claude:event result] {"duration_api_ms":11467,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d8631d98-ac51-4dcd-b988-6c0ba25ff26a","total_cost_usd":0.0079356,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":802,"cache_read_input_tokens":12921,"output_tokens":909,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":373},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":802},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":9,"output_tokens":909,"cache_read_input_tokens":12921,"cache_creation_input_tokens":802,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":802,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":1017,"outputTokens":14,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0010869999999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-haiku-4-5":{"inputTokens":9,"outputTokens":909,"cacheReadInputTokens":12921,"cacheCreationInputTokens":802,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0068486,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":373,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I'll help you set up a git server with automatic deployment to a web server. Here's a complete setup:\n\n## Server-side Configuration\n\n**1. Create a bare git repository**\n```bash\nmkdir -p /git/server\ncd /git/server\ngit init --bare\n```\n\n**2. Create a post-receive hook for automatic deployment**\n\nCreate `/git/server/hooks/post-receive`:\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nDEPLOY_DIR=\"/var/www/html\"\nmkdir -p $DEPLOY_DIR\ncd $DEPLOY_DIR\ngit clone --bare /git/server .git\ngit config --bool core.bare false\ngit reset --hard HEAD\n```\n\nMake it executable:\n```bash\nchmod +x /git/server/hooks/post-receive\n```\n\n**3. Set up the web server**\n\nStart a simple Python HTTP server on port 8080:\n```bash\nmkdir -p /var/www/html\ncd /var/www/html\npython3 -m http.server 8080\n```\n\nOr use nginx (more production-ready). Create `/etc/nginx/sites-available/default`:\n```nginx\nserver {\n    listen 8080 default_server;\n    server_name _;\n    root /var/www/html;\n    index index.html;\n    location / {\n        try_files $uri $uri/ =404;\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThen start nginx:\n```bash\nsudo systemctl start nginx\n```\n\n## Client-side Workflow\n\nOnce set up, your workflow becomes:\n```bash\ngit clone user@server:/git/server my-project\ncd my-project\necho \"hello world\" > hello.html\ngit add hello.html\ngit commit -m \"add hello.html\"\ngit push origin master\n```\n\nThen test:\n```bash\ncurl http://server:8080/hello.html\n```\n\n**Key points:**\n- The bare repository at `/git/server` acts as the central remote\n- The `post-receive` hook automatically checks out to `/var/www/html` whenever you push\n- The web server serves files from `/var/www/html`\n- This is a simple \"push-to-deploy\" system\n\nWould you like me to adjust this for a different web server setup, or do you need help with any specific part?","ttft_ms":5264,"type":"result","duration_ms":10156,"uuid":"c83c17b8-9d07-4586-915d-00e39f8911df","ttft_stream_ms":1076,"time_to_request_ms":45,"queued_turn_count":0}
